meta {
  name: Session Actions - Decide
  type: http
  seq: 73
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/v1/workspaces/:workspace/agents/:agent/sessions/:session/actions/decisions
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

params:path {
  workspace: {{workspaceId}}
  agent: {{agentId}}
  session: {{agentSessionId}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "decisions": [
      {
        "action_id": "{{agentActionId}}",
        "decision": "approve",
        "note": "Looks right.",
        "remember": false
      }
    ]
  }
}

docs {
  Decides waiting actions from an open chat. Requires the `agent.chat`
  permission. Every `action_id` must belong to this conversation or one of
  its subagents, or the whole call answers `404`. An action you may not
  decide (its tool names other approvers) answers `403`.

  - `decisions` — required, 1 to 100 entries:
    - `action_id` — required uuid, distinct.
    - `decision` — `approve`, `edit` (run with `arguments` instead) or
      `reject`.
    - `arguments` — object, required when `decision` is `edit`.
    - `note` — optional, max 2000; told to the agent on a rejection.
    - `stop` — optional bool; on `reject`, ends the agent's turn there.
    - `remember` — optional bool; on `approve`/`edit`, lets the tool run
      without asking from now on (ignored without `agent.manage`).

  Idempotent: an action no longer pending is skipped. When this leaves the
  conversation's paused turn fully decided it resumes on the queue and
  streams over Reverb as in `Sessions - Send Message (Reverb)`.

  Response is wrapped:
  `{ success, statusCode, message, data: { actions, resumed, run_id } }`.
}
